---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "How to Measure Your Typing Speed and Accuracy - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "How words per minute is calculated, why accuracy matters as much as speed, and how to get a fair typing score.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/how-to-measure-your-typing-speed.html">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Productivity</p>
    <h1>How to Measure Your Typing Speed and Accuracy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Typing speed is usually given in words per minute, but a fast score with many mistakes does not help much. A fair test measures both speed and accuracy.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>How words per minute is counted</h2>
<p>Most tests count five characters as one word, spaces included. The number of characters divided by five, then divided by the minutes taken, gives the words per minute. A 100-character passage typed in one minute scores 20 words per minute.</p>
<h2>Accuracy</h2>
<p>Accuracy is the share of characters that match the passage. Typing 95 of 100 characters correctly is 95% accuracy. Speed with low accuracy is slower in real work, because corrections take time.</p>
<h2>Get a fair score</h2>
<ul>
<li>Type from the screen rather than copying and pasting. Pasting makes the time meaningless.</li>
<li>Use the same passage and keyboard when you compare results.</li>
<li>Take several tests and look at the average, since one run can be unusual.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>The <a href="/tools/typing-speed-test.html">Typing Speed Test</a> starts the timer with your first key and shows words per minute and accuracy when you finish.</p>
